=== AGENT (turn 2) — 44.4s, in=5 out=2097, 2 tool calls ===
Done. The Evaluate Weather script is now much leaner:

```js
var current = $vars.fetchWeather1.output.body.current;
var temp = current.temperature_2m;
var weatherCode = current.weathercode;
var isNiceDay = temp >= 60 && temp <= 85 && weatherCode <= 2;
var message = isNiceDay ? 'Nice day in Bellevue.' : 'Not a nice day in Bellevue.';
return { isNiceDay: isNiceDay, message: message };
```

Two checks (temperature 60–85°F, clear sky), two short messages. Output is just `isNiceDay` (boolean) and `message` (string). Validates clean. What would you like to do next?

